---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const baseCodes = [
  ['R', 'A / G'], ['Y', 'C / T'], ['S', 'G / C'], ['W', 'A / T'],
  ['K', 'G / T'], ['M', 'A / C'], ['B', 'C / G / T'],
  ['D', 'A / G / T'], ['H', 'A / C / T'], ['V', 'A / C / G'], ['N', 'Any base'],
];
---

<BaseLayout>
  <header>
    <h1 id="pageTitle">SangerAnalyst</h1>
    <p>Turns raw chromatogram assemblies into a clean sequence — in one click.</p>
  </header>

  <main>
    <div class="card" aria-labelledby="pageTitle">
      <div class="upload-section" id="uploadSection">
        <div class="ab1-row">
          <div class="drop-slot" id="dropZoneF">
            <label for="fileF">Forward read (.ab1)</label>
            <input id="fileF" type="file" accept=".ab1" />
          </div>

          <button
            class="swap-btn"
            id="swapReadsBtn"
            type="button"
            title="Swap Forward and Reverse .ab1 files"
            aria-label="Swap Forward and Reverse reads"
          >⇄</button>

          <div class="drop-slot" id="dropZoneR">
            <label for="fileR">Reverse read (.ab1)</label>
            <input id="fileR" type="file" accept=".ab1" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="drop-hint">
          Tip: drag &amp; drop one or both <code>.ab1</code> files onto this card to auto-pair Forward &amp; Reverse reads.
        </div>

        <div class="row">
          <div style="flex:1">
            <div class="primer-header">
              <label id="primerF-label" for="primerF-text">Forward primer (optional, .fasta)</label>
              <div class="primer-actions">
                <button class="toggle-btn" data-target="F" type="button" title="Switch between paste sequence and upload file" aria-label="Toggle Forward primer input mode">📁</button>
                <button class="reset-btn" data-target="F" type="button" title="Clear Forward primer" aria-label="Clear Forward primer">⨉</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <input id="primerF-file" type="file" accept=".fasta,.fa,.fna,.txt" style="display:none;" />
            <input id="primerF-text" class="text-primer" type="text" maxlength="5000000" placeholder="Enter forward primer sequence (5' → 3')" style="display:block;"/>
          </div>
          <div style="flex:1">
            <div class="primer-header">
              <label id="primerR-label" for="primerR-text">Reverse primer (optional, .fasta)</label>
              <div class="primer-actions">
                <button class="toggle-btn" data-target="R" type="button" title="Switch between paste sequence and upload file" aria-label="Toggle Reverse primer input mode">📁</button>
                <button class="reset-btn" data-target="R" type="button" title="Clear Reverse primer" aria-label="Clear Reverse primer">⨉</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <input id="primerR-file" type="file" accept=".fasta,.fa,.fna,.txt" style="display:none;" />
            <input id="primerR-text" class="text-primer" type="text" maxlength="5000000" placeholder="Enter reverse primer sequence (5' → 3')" style="display:block;"/>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row">
          <div style="flex:1">
            <label for="mottCutoff">
              Mott Trim Cutoff
            </label>
            <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center;">
              <input id="mottCutoff" type="number" step="0.001" min="0.001" max="1" value="0.1" />
              <button class="info-btn" id="mottInfoBtn" type="button" aria-label="Mott cutoff info" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="m_tooltip">ℹ️</button>
            </div>
            <div class="small">
              Lower values remove more low-quality bases (shaded on the chromatograms).
            </div>
          </div>

          <div style="flex:1">
            <label for="qPhred">
              Min Base Phred Quality
            </label>
            <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center;">
              <input id="qPhred" type="number" step="1" min="1" max="70" value="20" />
              <button class="info-btn" id="qPhredInfoBtn" type="button" aria-label="Phred threshold info" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="q_tooltip">ℹ️</button>
            </div>
            <div class="small">
              Bases below this score are masked as “N” — including conflicts where both strands are low-quality.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <label for="secPeak">Secondary peak threshold (%)</label>
          <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center;">
            <input id="secPeak" type="number" step="1" min="1" max="100" value="33" />
            <button class="info-btn" id="secPeakInfoBtn" type="button" aria-label="Secondary peak info" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sec_tooltip">ℹ️</button>
          </div>
          <div class="small">
            Secondary peaks reaching this percentage of the primary peak’s height are marked (<span style="color:#d97706">◆</span>).
          </div>
          <div class="small">
            Mixed bases supported by secondary peaks are represented with <button class="text-info-btn" id="iupacInfoBtn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="iupac_tooltip">IUPAC ambiguity codes</button>.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="analyze-row">
          <button class="primary" id="analyzeBtn" type="button">Analyze</button>
          <button class="secondary" id="loadDemoBtn" type="button" title="Load the bundled control dataset">Try demo data</button>
        </div>
        <div id="loading" style="display:none; text-align:center; margin-top:20px;">
          <div class="dna-spinner"></div>
          <p>Processing…</p>
        </div>

        <div id="status" class="small" role="status" style="margin-top:10px;color:var(--muted)"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="trace-section" id="traceSection" style="display:none">
        <div class="trace-head">
          <div class="trace-title-group">
            <div class="trace-title">Input chromatograms</div>
          </div>
          <div class="trace-controls">
            <button class="trace-btn" id="traceZoomOut" type="button" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
            <button class="trace-btn" id="traceZoomIn" type="button" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
            <button class="trace-btn" id="traceReset" type="button" aria-label="Reset view">Reset</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="traceReview" class="trace-review" tabindex="-1" hidden>
          <p id="traceReviewLabel" role="status"></p>
          <button id="returnToResult" class="trace-btn" type="button">Back to result ↓</button>
        </div>
        <div class="trace-body">
          <div class="trace-stack">
            <div class="trace-row">
              <div class="trace-label" id="traceLabelF">Forward</div>
              <div class="trace-wrap"><canvas id="traceCanvasF" height="190"></canvas></div>
            </div>
            <div class="trace-row">
              <div class="trace-label" id="traceLabelR">Reverse</div>
              <div class="trace-wrap"><canvas id="traceCanvasR" height="190"></canvas></div>
            </div>
            <div class="trace-scroll" id="traceScrollBar" aria-label="Trace position">
              <div class="trace-scroll-spacer"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="trace-amp">
            <input type="range" id="traceAmp" min="0.5" max="4" step="0.1" value="1" aria-label="Peak height" />
            <span class="small">Peak<br/>height</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="trace-scaling">
          <label for="traceScale">Peak scaling</label>
          <select id="traceScale">
            <option value="balanced">Balance typical peaks</option>
            <option value="all">Fit all peaks</option>
          </select>
          <span>Each read uses one linear scale for all four bases.</span>
        </div>
        <p id="traceScaleNote" class="trace-scale-note" role="status" hidden>▲ Tall peaks exceed the display. Choose “Fit all peaks” to see their full height.</p>
        <p id="tracePeakStatus" class="small">Analyze to detect secondary peaks.</p>
        <div id="tracePeakInspector" class="trace-peak-inspector" hidden>
          <div class="trace-peak-heading">Secondary peaks in input reads</div>
          <div class="trace-peak-picker">
            <label for="tracePeakSelect">Choose a peak</label>
            <select id="tracePeakSelect"><option value="">Choose a peak</option></select>
          </div>
          <p id="tracePeakPrompt">Select a ◆ in a chromatogram or choose a peak to inspect its bases.</p>
          <div id="tracePeakDetail" class="trace-peak-detail" hidden>
            <span id="tracePeakPosition"></span>
            <span class="trace-peak-bases"><span>Primary <strong id="tracePrimaryBase"></strong></span><span>Secondary <strong id="traceSecondaryBase"></strong></span></span>
            <span id="tracePeakRatio"></span>
          </div>
          <p class="trace-peak-note">Peak height is shown as a percentage of the primary peak.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="traceWarn" class="trace-warn" style="display:none" role="alert"></div>
        <div class="small trace-meta">
          <span id="traceMeta"></span>
          <ul class="trace-legend" aria-label="Chromatogram legend">
            <li>Base colors: <span class="trace-base-legend"><span style="color:#16a34a">A</span> <span style="color:#2563eb">C</span> <span style="color:#111827">G</span> <span style="color:#dc2626">T</span></span></li>
            <li><span class="trace-peak-symbol">◆</span> Secondary peak</li>
            <li><span class="trace-trim-swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span> Shaded: Mott trimmed region</li>
            <li>Scroll to zoom, drag to pan.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="result-section" id="results" style="display:none">
        <h3 class="results-heading">Analysis results</h3>
        <p class="result-tabs-hint">Choose an output to view its sequence and alignment. Secondary-peak detection is shared below.</p>
        <p id="staleResultNotice" role="status" hidden>Inputs changed. Run Analyze again to update these results before exporting or inspecting traces.</p>
        <div id="server-warn" class="server-warn" role="alert" hidden></div>
        <p id="primerOutcome" class="small" style="white-space:pre-line" hidden></p>
        <div class="result-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Consensus outputs">
          <button id="strictTab" class="result-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="strictPanel" data-output="strict" type="button">High confidence</button>
          <button id="fullTab" class="result-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="fullPanel" data-output="full" tabindex="-1" type="button">Full merge</button>
          <button id="primerTrimTab" class="result-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="primerResultBlock" data-output="primerTrim" tabindex="-1" type="button" hidden>Primer trimmed</button>
        </div>
        <div id="strictPanel" class="result-block" data-output-panel="strict" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="strictTab" tabindex="0">
          <h4 class="result-title">High-confidence consensus</h4>
          <p class="result-hint">Sequence from the statistically validated overlapping region of both reads.</p>
          <div class="sequence-toolbar">
            <span class="output-label">Consensus sequence (FASTA)</span>
            <div class="result-controls">
              <button class="result-btn result-btn-primary copy-fasta-btn" data-target="strict" type="button">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/>
                  <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/>
                </svg>
                Copy FASTA
              </button>
              <button class="result-btn result-btn-primary download-fasta-btn" data-target="strict" type="button">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/>
                  <path d="M7 10l5 5 5-5"/>
                  <path d="M12 15V3"/>
                </svg>
                Download .fasta
              </button>
              <button class="result-btn blast-btn" data-target="strict" type="button" title="Copy this FASTA and open NCBI BLASTn in a new tab">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3h7v7M10 14 21 3M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg>
                NCBI BLASTn
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <pre id="strict" class="sequence-output" aria-label="High-confidence consensus FASTA" tabindex="0"></pre>
          <div class="sequence-footer">
            <span class="small">Sequence direction: 5′ → 3′</span>
          </div>
          <p class="small blast-help" id="strictBlastStatus" role="status">BLAST copies the FASTA and opens NCBI. Paste it into the query field.</p>
          <div class="alignment-block">
            <h4 class="alignment-title">Final read alignment</h4>
            <p class="small coordinate-note">Positions start at 1 within the overlapping portion of each oriented read.</p>
            <div id="strictReadCoverage"></div>
            <dl id="strictAlignmentStats" class="alignment-stats"></dl>
            <div id="strictConflicts" class="conflict-review"></div>
            <pre id="strictReport" class="alignment-output" aria-label="Final read alignment" tabindex="0"></pre>
            <div class="alignment-key" aria-label="Base highlighting legend"><span><code class="aln-mismatch">A</code> Mismatch</span><span><code class="amb">R</code> Mixed base</span><span aria-label="Uncalled bases"><code class="uncalled">NNNN</code></span><span><code class="aln-gap">–</code> Gap</span><span><code>|</code> Match</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="report-actions">
            <span class="report-label">Complete analysis report</span>
            <div class="result-controls">
              <button class="result-btn copy-btn" data-target="strict" type="button">Copy Report</button>
              <button class="result-btn download-btn" data-target="strict" type="button">Download Report (.txt)</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="fullPanel" class="result-block" data-output-panel="full" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="fullTab" tabindex="0" hidden>
          <h4 class="result-title">Full merged consensus</h4>
          <div class="result-hint">
            Complete merged span. Bases outside the validated overlap are supported by one read.
          </div>
          <div class="sequence-toolbar">
            <span class="output-label">Consensus sequence (FASTA)</span>
            <div class="result-controls">
              <button class="result-btn result-btn-primary copy-fasta-btn" data-target="full" type="button">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/>
                  <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/>
                </svg>
                Copy FASTA
              </button>
              <button class="result-btn result-btn-primary download-fasta-btn" data-target="full" type="button">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/>
                  <path d="M7 10l5 5 5-5"/>
                  <path d="M12 15V3"/>
                </svg>
                Download .fasta
              </button>
              <button class="result-btn blast-btn" data-target="full" type="button" title="Copy this FASTA and open NCBI BLASTn in a new tab">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3h7v7M10 14 21 3M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg>
                NCBI BLASTn
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p id="fullEmpty" class="small" hidden>No merged sequence is available. Check your input reads and the full report.</p>
          <pre id="full" class="sequence-output" aria-label="Full merged consensus FASTA" tabindex="0"></pre>
          <div class="sequence-footer">
            <span class="small">Sequence direction: 5′ → 3′</span>
          </div>
          <p class="small blast-help" id="fullBlastStatus" role="status">BLAST copies the FASTA and opens NCBI. Paste it into the query field.</p>
          <div class="alignment-block">
            <h4 class="alignment-title">Final read alignment</h4>
            <p class="small coordinate-note">Positions start at 1 within each quality-trimmed, oriented read. Terminal gaps indicate single-read coverage.</p>
            <div id="fullReadCoverage"></div>
            <dl id="fullAlignmentStats" class="alignment-stats"></dl>
            <div id="fullConflicts" class="conflict-review"></div>
            <pre id="fullReport" class="alignment-output" aria-label="Final read alignment" tabindex="0"></pre>
            <div class="alignment-key" aria-label="Base highlighting legend"><span><code class="aln-mismatch">A</code> Mismatch</span><span><code class="amb">R</code> Mixed base</span><span aria-label="Uncalled bases"><code class="uncalled">NNNN</code></span><span><code class="aln-gap">–</code> Gap</span><span><code>|</code> Match</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="report-actions">
            <span class="report-label">Complete analysis report</span>
            <div class="result-controls">
              <button class="result-btn copy-btn" data-target="full" type="button">Copy Report</button>
              <button class="result-btn download-btn" data-target="full" type="button">Download Report (.txt)</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="primerResultBlock" class="result-block" data-output-panel="primerTrim" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="primerTrimTab" tabindex="0" hidden>
          <h4 class="result-title">Primer-trimmed consensus</h4>
          <p class="result-hint">Consensus after primer trimming. Any fallback trimming is flagged above.</p>
          <div class="sequence-toolbar">
            <span class="output-label">Consensus sequence (FASTA)</span>
            <div class="result-controls">
              <button class="result-btn result-btn-primary copy-fasta-btn" data-target="primerTrim" type="button">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/>
                  <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/>
                </svg>
                Copy FASTA
              </button>
              <button class="result-btn result-btn-primary download-fasta-btn" data-target="primerTrim" type="button">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/>
                  <path d="M7 10l5 5 5-5"/>
                  <path d="M12 15V3"/>
                </svg>
                Download .fasta
              </button>
              <button class="result-btn blast-btn" data-target="primerTrim" type="button" title="Copy this FASTA and open NCBI BLASTn in a new tab">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 3h7v7M10 14 21 3M21 14v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5"/></svg>
                NCBI BLASTn
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p id="primerTrimEmpty" class="small" hidden>No primer-trimmed sequence is available. Check primer matches in the full report.</p>
          <pre id="primerTrim" class="sequence-output" aria-label="Primer-trimmed consensus FASTA" tabindex="0"></pre>
          <div class="sequence-footer">
            <span class="small">Sequence direction: 5′ → 3′</span>
          </div>
          <p class="small blast-help" id="primerTrimBlastStatus" role="status">BLAST copies the FASTA and opens NCBI. Paste it into the query field.</p>
          <section class="alignment-block primer-bindings" aria-labelledby="primerBindingTitle">
            <h4 id="primerBindingTitle" class="alignment-title">Primer binding sites</h4>
            <div id="primerBindingResults"></div>
          </section>
          <div class="alignment-block">
            <h4 class="alignment-title">Read alignment after primer trimming</h4>
            <p class="small coordinate-note">Only the retained sequence is shown. Read positions refer to the quality-trimmed, oriented reads.</p>
            <dl id="primerTrimAlignmentStats" class="alignment-stats"></dl>
            <div id="primerTrimConflicts" class="conflict-review"></div>
            <pre id="primerTrimReport" class="alignment-output" aria-label="Read alignment after primer trimming" tabindex="0"></pre>
            <div class="alignment-key" aria-label="Base highlighting legend"><span><code class="aln-mismatch">A</code> Mismatch</span><span><code class="amb">R</code> Mixed base</span><span aria-label="Uncalled bases"><code class="uncalled">NNNN</code></span><span><code class="aln-gap">–</code> Gap</span><span><code>|</code> Match</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="report-actions">
            <span class="report-label">Complete analysis report</span>
            <div class="result-controls">
              <button class="result-btn copy-btn" data-target="primerTrim" type="button">Copy Report</button>
              <button class="result-btn download-btn" data-target="primerTrim" type="button">Download Report (.txt)</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <section class="peak-section shared-peaks" aria-labelledby="peakHeading">
          <h4 id="peakHeading" class="result-title">Secondary-peak detection</h4>
          <p class="small"><span id="peakCoordinateContext"></span></p>
          <p id="peakThreshold" class="small"></p>
          <div id="sharedPeaks"></div>
          <p class="small peak-coordinate-note">Trace positions follow the read orientation stated in the report. Peaks outside the selected sequence are excluded.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <h3>How Does It Work?</h3>
      <p class="small" style="margin-top:8px">
        SangerAnalyst trims low-quality regions with Mott's algorithm, verifies the forward–reverse overlap is statistically real, aligns the reads and builds a quality-weighted consensus — sequencing errors are corrected from the higher-quality strand, while disagreements corroborated by secondary peaks are kept as IUPAC ambiguity codes. Primer &amp; off-target regions are then trimmed away for a clean final report. <br/><br/> Powered by Biopython — trusted library for sequence processing and alignment.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="how" id="faq">
      <h3>FAQ</h3>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            What file types does SangerAnalyst support?
            <svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Applied Biosystems <code>.ab1</code> chromatogram files for the forward and reverse reads. Primers are optional — upload them as FASTA (<code>.fasta</code>, <code>.fa</code>, <code>.fna</code>, <code>.txt</code>) or paste the sequence directly.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Is SangerAnalyst free to use?
            <svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes — completely free, no account, nothing to install. Upload your chromatograms and download the results.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            How does it merge forward and reverse reads?
            <svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Reads are trimmed with Mott's algorithm, oriented automatically, aligned, and combined into a quality-weighted consensus. Sequencing errors are corrected from the higher-quality strand, and the overlap is statistically validated before the high-confidence consensus is produced.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Can it detect heterozygotes or mixed templates?
            <svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. Secondary peaks above your threshold that corroborate a forward–reverse disagreement are called as IUPAC ambiguity codes (R, Y, K, M, S, W) in the consensus — the same principle behind PolyPhred-style mutation detection.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Does it work with longer amplicons like 16S rRNA (~1,500 bp)?
            <svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. With ~900 bp reads sharing ~300 bp of overlap, the High-Confidence Consensus covers the validated overlap while the Full Merge reconstructs the entire ~1,500 bp span. Primer trimming then yields the longest methodologically reliable sequence.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Do I need to install anything?
            <svg class="chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>No. Open the page, drop in your chromatograms, and download the results.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

